                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0f7caa47-56e1-3c48-b36b-d0f18d8a34f5",
                        "entry_id": "2c8014f5-8ffe-3938-ad64-bbf791837766",
                        "glosses": [
                            "фин. косвенный налог (преимущественно на предметы массового потребления, а также услуги), включаемый в цену товаров или тарифы на услуги"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb5a188a-865f-4037-a170-5022a4166338",
                                "sense_id": "0f7caa47-56e1-3c48-b36b-d0f18d8a34f5",
                                "text": "Скажем, табачный акциз составляет в Ярославской области почти два миллиарда рублей."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db55272d-5ed1-347d-9e16-7116ed388460",
                        "entry_id": "2c8014f5-8ffe-3938-ad64-bbf791837766",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. учреждение в царской России, ведавшее акцизными сборами"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7af18648-9aeb-4fb6-9097-8edc253ed1dd",
                                "sense_id": "db55272d-5ed1-347d-9e16-7116ed388460",
                                "text": "Он действительно был сыном мелкого чиновника, до революции служившего в акцизе, и действительно никогда ни в чём «не был замешан»."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0542393f-818e-44b5-ab59-eaa28a80da1f",
                        "source_entry_id": "2c8014f5-8ffe-3938-ad64-bbf791837766",
                        "source_sense_description": "налог",
                        "target_lang_word": "excise",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "excise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d66a0bc-1349-346b-adb5-029833b40709",
                                        "entry_id": "f50f0699-d9d5-3d86-a699-e83163bf8932",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tax charged on goods produced within the country (as opposed to customs duties, charged on goods from outside the country)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22280150-4a42-4a8a-9b2c-40b863cad5c0",
                                                "sense_id": "9d66a0bc-1349-346b-adb5-029833b40709",
                                                "text": "Andrew Houſtoun and Adam Muſhet, being Tackſmen of the Excize, did Imploy Thomas Rue to be their Collector, and gave him a Sallary of 30. pound Sterling for a year."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40fcf700-e912-4d82-ac20-ddc8e89955f3",
                                                "sense_id": "9d66a0bc-1349-346b-adb5-029833b40709",
                                                "text": "1755, Samuel Johnson, A Dictionary of the English Language, \"excise\",\nA hateful tax levied upon commodities, and adjudged not by the common judges of property, but wretches hired by those to whom Excise is paid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f98c56e-b905-4192-b949-afecd1cd4b5d",
                                                "sense_id": "9d66a0bc-1349-346b-adb5-029833b40709",
                                                "text": "1787, Constitution of the United States of America, Article I, Section 8,\nThe Congress shall have power to lay and collect taxes, duties, imposts, and excises, to pay the debts […] of the United States;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "excise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "755fbece-bf3f-3588-981a-4a93f300b4ad",
                                        "entry_id": "3eeff816-e8a8-39fa-ba03-6443d4c778f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To impose an excise tax on something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "excise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffbbd56f-f560-3fa9-9e95-599a4b384dc3",
                                        "entry_id": "700c22a9-c1e7-36f7-810d-6661be7f61e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut out; to remove."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "646209b2-9d9f-40bb-ae45-b2f85a715957",
                                                "sense_id": "ffbbd56f-f560-3fa9-9e95-599a4b384dc3",
                                                "text": "[T]hey [warts] may be lifted up with the forceps, and excised with a knife or scissors, and the wound touched with nitrate of silver."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a9bb749-7d24-4776-9233-ecbb8fd3e772",
                                                "sense_id": "ffbbd56f-f560-3fa9-9e95-599a4b384dc3",
                                                "text": "1901, Andrew Lang, Preface to the second edition of Myth, Ritual, and Religion,\nIn revising the book I […] have excised certain passages which, as the book first appeared, were inconsistent with its main thesis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dda60396-ec7d-4105-a59f-544d47f71871",
                                                "sense_id": "ffbbd56f-f560-3fa9-9e95-599a4b384dc3",
                                                "text": "In the opposite direction the allowance of 103 min. for the 83.8 miles from Waterloo to Salisbury, which has remained untouched since the worst period in the war, when it included a Woking stop that long since has been excised, was another timing that left drivers completely nonplussed at times as to how to fill it out."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84fcc58-0fd6-442a-8997-3569b955d760",
                                                "sense_id": "ffbbd56f-f560-3fa9-9e95-599a4b384dc3",
                                                "text": "Insanity can be cured. Personality disorders are so inextricably entwined with the heart and mind and soul that it is well-nigh impossible to excise them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c2398d2-24c0-4cd7-a766-3ff9ecf5cc18",
                                                "sense_id": "ffbbd56f-f560-3fa9-9e95-599a4b384dc3",
                                                "text": "A person is guilty of an offence if he excises, infibulates or otherwise mutilates the whole or any part of a girl’s labia majora, labia minora or clitoris."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
